From ea3344f749a3234412e4a16a78459ace659f46b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.local>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:45:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Sort imports in 35 test modules so the box can push again

The trading box is 493 commits ahead of origin and NOT ONE of them could leave.
ops/githooks/pre-push runs the gates and refuses on RED, and the gates have been RED
on 35 I001 findings -- unsorted imports, one per file, every one in tests/scripts/
and every one ruff-fixable. Nothing on the money path, nothing anyone had to think
about, and it stranded several days of fixes on one machine.

That is also the mechanism behind the revert the cycle builder hit: Adopt-Release
lands ORIGIN's tree in place, so with origin 493 commits stale, box work that had not
been pushed was overwritten by a tree predating it. The wedged git-credential-manager
chains were downstream, not the cause -- a push the hook refuses still leaves its
helper processes behind to be reaped.

Fixed with `ruff check --fix` on exactly those paths. ruff clean, mypy clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WZHzZoD3QX9Tx668fkAaw6
